module fluorescence

manifest leaf_tissue
manifest trichloroacetic_acid
manifest tba_reagent

instructions:

// Step 1: Grind leaf tissue (control or infected) with liquid nitrogen, then homogenize
// 100 mg powder with 1 mL of 0.1% (w/v) TCA
tissue = dispense 100 units of leaf_tissue
tca = dispense 1000 units of trichloroacetic_acid
homogenate = mix tissue with tca

// Step 2: Centrifugation (12,000 x g, 15 min, 4 C) is off-chip; supernatant is carried forward

// Step 3: Combine 1 mL of 0.5% TBA in 20% TCA with 0.5 mL of the supernatant
tba = dispense 1000 units of tba_reagent
reaction = mix homogenate with tba

// Step 4: Heat at 95 C for 30 min (dry bath), then cool at ice-cold temperature
heat reaction at 95c for 30m
heat reaction at 4c for 5m

// Step 5: Second centrifugation (14,000 x g, 15 min, 4 C) is off-chip; supernatant carried forward

// Step 6: Measure absorbance at 532 nm (TBARS signal) and 600 nm (turbidity correction);
// A600 is subtracted from A532 downstream to give corrected absorbance
// (detect fluorescence used as the generic optical-signal readout stand-in, since BioScript
// exposes no dedicated absorbance/spectrophotometric detect module)
abs_532 = detect fluorescence on reaction for 30s
abs_600 = detect fluorescence on reaction for 30s

dispose reaction
